From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:06:42 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: Implement xdg-decoration-unstable-v1

Add the zxdg_decoration_manager_v1 global (version 2), so a client can
ask for server-side decorations for its xdg_toplevel instead of drawing
its own titlebar.

The effective mode is decided by the new org.gnome.mutter.wayland
"decoration-mode" key: "client-preference" (the default) honours
set_mode, and picks server-side decorations after unset_mode or when the
client never set one; "server-side" and "client-side" force the mode for
every client that binds the protocol. Clients that do not create a
decoration object keep client-side decorations, so GTK and libadwaita
apps are unaffected.

The mode is part of MetaWaylandWindowConfiguration. It goes out as
zxdg_toplevel_decoration_v1.configure right before the xdg_toplevel
configure that carries it, and applies when that configure is acked.
set_mode and unset_mode are always answered with a configure, as are
decoration objects created for an already configured toplevel
(version 2), and a policy change reconfigures the windows whose mode
changes. A destroyed decoration object switches back to client-side
decorations at the next commit.

A server-side decorated window's frame rect includes the decoration (a
titlebar, and a border while floating): finish_move_resize grows the
client's window geometry by the decoration borders, making the frame
extents negative, and the xdg_toplevel configure and bounds are shrunk
by the same borders. Placement, constraints, maximization, tiling and
min/max size hints therefore work on the decorated frame, like an X11
frame. Popup anchor rects and xdg_popup.configure positions are offset
so they stay relative to the parent's window geometry.

Errors: already_constructed, unconfigured_buffer for version 1 objects,
invalid_mode, and orphaned for requests on a decoration whose
xdg_toplevel is gone.

The decoration is not drawn yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
